ts.file<pre><code>  rowClassRules is just like cellClassRules — but it applies CSS classes to entire rows,
  instead of individual cells.
Purpose:
To dynamically style full rows based on conditions in your data.
 Basic Syntax:
 rowClassRules: {
  'row-error': params =&gt; params.data.status === 'error',
  'row-success': params =&gt; params.data.status === 'success'
}

----html----
&lt;ag-grid-angular
  class="ag-theme-alpine"
  [rowData]="rowData"
  [columnDefs]="columnDefs"
  [rowClassRules]="rowClassRules"&gt;//rowClassRules
&lt;/ag-grid-angular&gt;

